today is the second week of in-person  learning for some ccsd students  it's just the start of the district's  plan to get everyone safely back on  campus before the end of the school year  we have bianca holman live with us this  morning with some concerns that parents  have  as the students transition back to class  bianca  hey good morning john so all ccsd staff  and teachers they'll be back on campus  in about a week and then in a few weeks  the fourth graders through 12th graders  and like we're here at bonanza high  school they'll be back in the classroom  but with that hybrid model some parents  they still have issues with it  and so of course they've been expressing  those concerns to us and  one potential problem is that ccsd is  selecting  student groups based on a survey parents  filled out that was back in september  the district says it needs to lock  things down like transportation plans  and doesn't have time to do another  survey  but as rebecca garcia of the nevada pta  points out  a lot of things have changed since then  and some families want to switch their  group from last year  more public health statistics have  changed the vaccine is now available and  all of us who filled it out in november  aren't getting a chance to change our  response  so secondary schools they're going to  follow that same hybrid model as the  elementary school  students of course being split into  three groups some go on campus monday  and tuesday others on thursday and  friday and then of course there's a  third group that stays learning online  from home but  even students who go to campus will only  take two classes in person and then  they'll finish the rest of  the rest of their classes remotely now  safety is still a big concern  we learned that last week there were  eight staff members who tested positive  for coronavirus  although the district did not say if  those individuals were  working remotely or if they were people  who are working from the campus and or  teaching students so that information  has not been shared with us  reporting live bianca holman 8 news now
 

